{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UxksSfWo9j3FRqu4RmfZtS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-25; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n5\t- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`), CUMULATIVE from D3: one group per past day (`dNN--sample.<ext>`, `variant-000`\n6\t  before D22) + ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF/MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET, D4 Go, D5 Rust, D6 Java jar,\n7\t  D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig (PE in Mastery), D11 D, D12 FPC, D13 Crystal, D14 ObjC, D15 C `-stripped`/\n8\t  `-symbolized`, D16 WASM `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay,\n9\t  D21 OCaml `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs`, D22 F# (+ `FSharp.Core.dll`), D23 VB.NET, D24 Scala jar PAIR `-vulnerable`/\n10\t  `-corrected`, **D25 Clojure jar PAIR** (same role names, ~8 KB each).\n11\t  Since D18 each day = a structure/behaviour THEME on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/overlays (D20),\n12\t  shared libraries (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), anti-analysis predicates (D23), PATCH DIFFING (D24 \"diff the vulnerable\n13\t  function against its corrected twin ... prove the old one was really broken\"), BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT CAUSE (D25 \"the code reaches\n14\t  where it shouldn't. Prove the bounds error is real, trace its reachability, and compare against the corrected twin\").\n15\t  D24-D25 = a VULN-RESEARCH arc on twins (null deref -> OOB read; next: another bug class -- integer overflow, UAF, format\n16\t  string, injection, race -- or a NATIVE twin). D22-D25 = \"new language on an old runtime\" 4x (F#, VB.NET, Scala, Clojure --\n17\t  predicted): Groovy is the last obvious JVM language (d07 still leaks \"Day 26 ... primary classfile named by that unit\"), then\n18\t  C++/CLI, Elixir/BEAM, Haxe->Neko.\n19\t  Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` (D15/D16/D21/D24/\n20\t  D25) and unqualified ids whose QUESTION names the member (D21) or demands consensus of both twins (D24/D25).\n21\t- From D2 every new member embeds the **HCFG** blob `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16le len | u32le crc32(plain) | xor'd JSON\n22\t  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (see Variant axes). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND base64 `SENGR...`, crc-gate every hit; when\n23\t  both miss, look past the image end (overlay) and read the question. The JSON has never-asked keys (ipv4, windows_path,\n24\t  linux_path, service, host_model): parse the whole dict.\n25\t- The analysis is easy; the hard part is the GM's label for `exact_text` fields. **The organizers RE-ISSUE the contract** when a\n26\t  label is unguessable (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> enum + ordered rules). Since D24 EVERY question is a full SPEC (sha256 \"ZIP\n27\t  central-directory order ... member K (1-based)\", format rule list, HCFG layout + carrier rule per container, JAR: \"Base64-\n28\t  alphabet UTF-8 constants of at least 80 characters ... first CRC32-valid\"). `format` enum d12+: `elf, pe, pe_cli, jar, wasm,\n29\t  neko_bytecode`.\n30\t- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19 named \"RS20 for Day 20\" (came true). Still open after D25: enum `neko_bytecode`, d07\n31\t  `method_count` \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit\". Grep each contract for `[A-Z]{2}\\d\\d`, `Day NN`,\n32\t  unseen enum values (D21-D25: nothing new).\n33\t- **Theme asked on its own group only sometimes**: D5-D18 never; D19 (`overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`), D20\n34\t  (`hcfg_resource_size`) yes; D21-D25 NO (twins: 2 sha256 + `<role>_format` + config_* x2). Imports/ImplMap/predicates/the\n35\t  D24-D25 diffs + triggers = backfill candidates (D17 precedent).\n36\t- **Every member embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) {branch, event_count, campaign, family\n37\t  `<lang>_<theme>_trace`, effects, network none} gated on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (analysis/sandbox/workstation). Recent:\n38\t  D23 `vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only` (+`analysis_detected`), D24 `scala_patch_diff_trace`/\n39\t  `benign_control_and_reversion_only` (+`control_positive`), D25 `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`/`bounded_synthetic_fault_only`\n40\t  (+ 2nd env var `HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT`).\n41\t- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160 (D16), D17 204 (backfill #2), then +12/day: D24 288, **D25 300**, no backfill since D17.\n42\t  Mastery = `setN.` copies (+1 set/day: D24 8 sets, **D25 9 sets = 2700 ids, ~36 MB per delivery**). Timed end to end: D23\n43\t  13.0 / 7.9 s; D24 5.0 / 8.4 s; **D25 TT 10.5 s; Mastery first POST 54 s INCORRECT (55 ids cross-wired, see Pitfalls), CORRECT\n44\t  ~2 min after start via localize + a live worker.**\n45\t\n46\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n47\t- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, storage per container: `.hcfg` section (D2/D10/D14), .NET FieldRVA (D3), Go/Rust\n48\t  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin, D24 Scala `$` module, D25 Clojure `<ns>__init.class` `encoded-config` Var)\n49\t  / Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW FPC `.data`, WASM data seg 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay, D20 RS20 overlay,\n50\t  D21 OCaml plugin `.data`, D22 F# RAW twice (`.text` + PE overlay: \"FIRST record that validates\"), D23 VB.NET RAW PE overlay.\n51\t  Rule: scan for `HCFG` and `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (jars: every class's constant pool), accept only crc32(plain) match AND\n52\t  parsing JSON, keep scanning past failures (D9 Nim decoys); never a fixed offset or a fixed class. Storage never changed WITHIN a day (single/TT/all Mastery sets).\n53\t- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- appended at `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize`, magic `<2 caps><day>`, header\n54\t  spelled by the QUESTION: PK19 `magic|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le packed_len @8|sha256(unpacked) @12|packed @44`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`;\n55\t  RS20 `magic|ver @4|u32le resource_len @8|u16le scratch_len @12|sha256(scratch) @16|HCFG @48 raw|scratch`. Rule: `o =\n56\t  data.rfind(magic)` (\"final\"), parse the listed widths, verify bounds + hash; unspecified transform -> known-plaintext `HCFG`.\n57\t- **Location / storage as answer** -- `hcfg_offset` = decimal FILE offset (base64 -> the `S`, RAW -> the `H`); `overlay_offset` =\n58\t  the magic, `overlay_size` = len - offset; `hcfg_resource_size` = the u32le @+8 (380). `hcfg_storage` (D17 enum) in order:\n59\t  `base64` -> `raw_hcfg_section` -> `wasm_data_segment` -> `raw_const_array` (other native data section) -> `raw`.\n60\t- **Any other encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data)`** (hex/base32/85/UTF-16/reversed/xor/zlib/multibyte+rolling xor/byte maps/\n61\t  custom b64/split/int-array/strided/RC4/AES/TEA/ChaCha/stack-built); `hcfg_find` = first valid hit. Not the PK19 stub.\n62\t- **xor key / config VALUE SHAPES** -- crc, key byte and campaign/domain/mutex/url re-roll per variant. Timed modes change the\n63\t  SHAPE too: D23 campaign `BRNN-00V` -> `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-CATALOG-00V` -> `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol\n64\t  `variant-000.c` -> `sample.c`; D24 also domain `node-00V.dayNN...` -> `<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid` (word: sync/hub/\n65\t  core/mesh/relay/stage, D25 also edge/cache/vault/proxy/node), mutex `Global\\HuntressBRNN_00V` -> `Global\\Huntress<12 uppercase\n66\t  hex>`, url `.../api/BRNN-00V` -> `https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>` (path words vault/edge/stage/sync/\n67\t  gate); the url host word is independent of the domain word. Rule: copy values verbatim from the decoded JSON/symtab; never\n68\t  regex-check a value shape or key on `00V` indices.\n69\t- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02, d04, d10 `pe`); labels from THIS member's header;\n70\t  dispatch on MAGIC (`7f454c46`, `MZ`, `PK`, `\\0asm`, next `NEKO`). PE symbol fields = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`. Extensions lie\n71\t  about role, not container (D21 `.cmxs` = ELF ET_DYN).\n72\t- **Member qualifier in the id (D15/D16/D21/D24)** -- peel the longest field prefix that is a `[^a-z0-9]+` token of exactly one\n73\t  member name (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`, `loader`/`plugin`, `vulnerable`/`corrected` D24+D25); the token can sit\n74\t  BEFORE the field family (D24 `d24_analysis_corrected_format`, `..._corrected_config_url`). `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order, never\n75\t  sorted (D24: vulnerable is member 1).\n76\t- **Member named in the QUESTION (D21)** -- after the qualifier peel, if >1 member remains, keep the one whose basename ends with\n77\t  the token after `basename ends` / `Use the dNN--`. ORDER MATTERS (running it first dropped 26 ids on D21).\n78\t- **Unqualified id over a twin pair (D24, D25 identical wording)** -- \"Decode both dNN-- role members and require their config objects to be\n79\t  byte-for-byte equal before using the common value\": decode EVERY member, assert equal JSON, answer the common value (a\n80\t  first-member pick also passed because the twins always shared the config, but a mismatch should raise, not guess).\n81\t- **Member basename vocabulary (D22)** -- `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`; group by `dNN--` + extension/role tag only.\n82\t- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly + `.runtimeconfig.json` (+ D22 `FSharp.Core.dll`); question:\n83\t  \"primary managed assembly ... runtimeconfig and dependency DLL members are delivery support only\". Primary = the `.dll` whose\n84\t  name is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*), i.e. the one carrying HCFG; hash ALL members.\n85\t- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets (D15-D17 Mastery, D17/D19 TT, D23 Mastery set6): symbols/\n86\t  disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none` (GM-confirmed; leaf-heuristic constants rejected). Pair by sha256.\n87\t- **Contract wording per fetch (D17)** -- question/answer_format of an id can change between fetches; read `answer_format` per id.\n88\t- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (2-9 sets; D25 9 x ~36 MB), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence\n89\t  case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT `dNN-tt-...`) = set->delivery map. **Member-bytes identity\n90\t  (D25)**: with 9 sets x ~34 members, per-member caches keyed on `id(bytes)` returned ANOTHER member's facts once the first was\n91\t  freed and CPython reused the address (5/9 sets wrong: d23 <- d03 config, d22/d15 <- d10 PE header, d06/d24 <- d16 wasm). Rule:\n92\t  key every per-member cache on (delivery, member name) or sha256, or keep the bytes alive for the whole run -- never `id()`.\n93\t- **kind for the same field name** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER (`64`/`62`) on d08/d15/d21: dispatch on kind.\n94\t- **Feature-presence / per-group field sets** -- `has_<x>` = a structural marker of <x> in THIS member (`has_hcfg_section`, D17\n95\t  `has_go_runtime` etc.); old groups gain ids over days (D8, D17): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.\n96\t- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- CPU contention: re-measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py`; D25 TT\n97\t  solve phase 8.0 s at 300 ids under load (single ~1.2 s isolated on D24).\n98\t\n99\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n100\t| You see | First move |\n101\t|---|---|\n102\t| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |\n103\t| `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -p .hu