n/System.Console,\n`StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_0`8`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (d03's bytes). Predicates (theme, UNASKED):\n`Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch.StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks` (clock), `Environment.get_ProcessorCount`,\n`GetEnvironmentVariable(\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\")` vs workstation/analysis/sandbox -> branch success/decoy/failure, trace\n`vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only`, field `analysis_detected`. No ImplMap, no FieldRVA. HCFG RAW ONCE as\na PE overlay right after `.reloc` (7680 = EOF-380). 276 ids = 264 + 12 (2 sha256 + d22 family + `xor_key_hex`). Carried-over\nsolver -> CORRECT T+84 s (22 s download), 0 wrong; TT 13.0 s / Mastery 7 sets (1932 ids) 7.9 s first try. NEW in timed modes:\nvalue SHAPES re-rolled (`BR23-<8 uppercase hex>` campaign, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `sample.c`) -- harmless\nfor a verbatim-copying solver. THIRD .NET language (C# D3, F# D22, VB.NET D23) and the first BEHAVIOUR (evasion) theme.\n**D24 \"Spot the Difference\" (patch-diffing)** = a Scala 2.13 TWIN pair: `d24--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1) +\n`d24--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2), ~4 KB each, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Scala factory`, classes\n`Day24<Role>000.class` (static forwarder, Main-Class) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` (module: `MODULE$`, base64 HCFG `ldc` in\n`<clinit>`, `decodeConfig`, `score(String)I`, `main`), `ScalaSignature`/`ScalaSig`, scala-library not bundled. Prompt: \"Two\nbuilds, one fix. Diff the vulnerable function against its corrected twin and pinpoint exactly what changed -- then prove the old\none was really broken.\" The fix (UNASKED): only `score` changed -- vulnerable `if (s.nonEmpty) s.charAt(0) else -1` NPEs on\n`null` (CWE-476); corrected `Option(s).filter(_.nonEmpty).map(_.charAt(0)).getOrElse(-1)` (+3 invokedynamic lambdas). `main`\nidentical (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL lookupswitch -> decoy/success/failure), trace `scala_patch_diff_trace`/`benign_control_and