rs and require their config objects to be\n72\t  byte-for-byte equal before using the common value\": decode EVERY member, assert equal JSON, answer the common value (a\n73\t  first-member pick also passed because the twins always shared the config, but a mismatch should raise, not guess).\n74\t- **Theme sidecar inside the member (D26)** -- the jar carries a non-class entry `crash/trace.json` = `{\"schema\":\n75\t  \"huntress.synthetic_crash.v1\",\"kind\":\"IllegalStateException\",\"frames\":[\"stageThree\",\"stageTwo\",\"stageOne\"]}` (innermost\n76\t  first). Values were IDENTICAL in all 12 deliveries (single, TT, 10 Mastery sets) while config re-rolled. Rule: open the\n77\t  member's zip, pick the entry whose name ends `trace.json` (never a fixed path), `json.loads`, answer frames[0] verbatim;\n78\t  predicates (\"every frame is in the primary classfile method-name set\") = set inclusion over method_info names; a missing\n79\t  sidecar = `none`/`false`. Expect the same sidecar idea in other containers (ELF section, PE resource, separate member).\n80\t- **Primary classfile (D7 vs D26)** -- d07 = manifest Main-Class; d26 \"primary classfile named by that unit\" = also the\n81\t  Main-Class (`Day26Variant000`, SourceFile `Day26Variant000.groovy`), NOT the `$_main_closure1` closure class. method_count =\n82\t  ALL method_info rows incl. Groovy synthetics (`<init>`, 3 stages, main, `$getStaticMetaClass`, get/setMetaClass, `$getLookup`,\n83\t  `getEncodedConfig` = 10). Inner class names keep `Variant000` although basenames say `sample`.\n84\t- **Member basename vocabulary (D22)** -- `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`; group by `dNN--` + extension/role tag only.\n85\t- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly + `.runtimeconfig.json` (+ D22 `FSharp.Core.dll`); question:\n86\t  \"primary managed assembly ... runtimeconfig and dependency DLL members are delivery support only\". Primary = the `.dll` whose\n87\t  name is not a framework/dependen