cording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10275bf2-3967-4c85-8fd5-58c86d81240b","uuid":"513b5200-9d50-49f6-8244-2b37987b9a08","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:11:04.141Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"id\": \"solver-member-cache-identity\", \"concept\": \"Per-member caches in the cumulative solver keyed on id(bytes) cross-wire members once Python reuses a freed object's address (D25 Mastery: 55 ids in 5/9 sets answered with another dNN-- group's facts)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/solver/solve.py keys _SHA/_ZIPS/_ISJAR/_FACTS/_CFG on id(b) (lines ~61-126, 303-317, 692, 872-891); with 9 sets x ~34 members the first daemon POST failed (d23 <- d03 config, d22/d15 <- d10 PE header, d06/d24 <- d16 wasm, d25 vulnerable <- d03 pe_cli). Fix before D26's timed modes: key on (delivery path, member name) or sha256, or hold every member's bytes in a list for the run; add a regression that runs a 9-set Mastery case (cases/variant-mastery-f395c0c5) with HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 and =1. Diagnostic rule: a rejected value that is a