{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQuRrvWkeqskYJiyQKiL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LVqyPUJC7zr6CrRpVsgTK4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=t.index('```json',i)+len('```json'); k=t.index('```',j)\ng=json.loads(t[j:k])\nbyid={x['id']:x for x in g}\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='groovy-script-class-facts']   # seen day26\nbyid['solver-member-cache-identity']['priority']=2\nbyid['solver-member-cache-identity']['detail']+=\" D26: the fix held -- Mastery 10 sets (3120 ids) and TT CORRECT first try; keep the regression and re-check after any set-count jump.\"\nbyid['contract-forward-hints']['detail']+=\" D26: the d07 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit' leak came TRUE (Groovy jar; the primary classfile = the manifest Main-Class `Day26Variant000`, not the `$_main_closure1` closure). Only `neko_bytecode` remains open; D26 contract added no new token/day.\"\nbyid['theme-facts-recording']['detail']+=\" D26: the theme WAS asked on its own day again (first since D20): crash_fault_method (trace.json frames[0]) + crash_frames_match_methods (frames subset of primary-class method names), read from a JSON sidecar entry inside the jar. Unasked D26 facts worth exposing for a backfill: trace kind (IllegalStateException), frame count/depth, static call chain stageOne->stageTwo->stageThree, throw site (new+athrow in stageThree), env gates HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL/HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT, trace family groovy_synthetic_crash_trace / bounded_caught_exception_only.\"\nfor x in ('clojure-namespace-facts','jvm-twin-diff-gensym-normalization','jni-java-native-bridge-pair'):\n    byid[x]['priority']=2\nF='challenges/day26/binary-crash-course/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d26--sample.jar'\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"crash-sidecar-generic-parser\",\"concept\":\"Crash/trace SIDECAR anywhere in a member (D26 shape generalised): locate a crash record in a jar/zip entry, ELF section or note, PE RCDATA/.NET resource, overlay or a separate `dNN--*.json`/`.txt` member, and expose its facts\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":f\"D26 asked crash_fault_method (= frames[0] verbatim) and crash_frames_match_methods (every frame in the primary classfile method-name set) from `crash/trace.json` = {{schema: huntress.synthetic_crash.v1, kind, frames[innermost..]}} inside {F}. Build lib.binary.crash_sidecar(member_bytes) -> {{schema, kind, frames, frame_count, fault_method, outer_method, raw}}: search zip entries whose name ends trace.json/crash*.json/*.trace, any JSON object with a `frames`/`stack`/`backtrace` list in raw bytes (ELF section, PE resource, overlay, UTF-16 too), and text traces. Normalise frame strings in every likely shape: bare `stageThree`, `Class.method`, `pkg.Class.method(File.groovy:12)`, `module!func+0x1a`, `func+0x1a/0x40`, `#0 0x... in func file:line`, raw `0x401136` (-> resolve via symtab). Predicates: frames subset of method set (JVM method_info names, .NET MethodDef names, ELF/PE FUNC symbols), frame[0] defined in the primary unit, frames form a valid static call chain (see jvm-call-chain-throw-site-facts). Missing sidecar -> `none`/`false`. Fixtures: the D26 jar + synthesised variants (renamed entry path, frames with descriptors, sidecar in an ELF section).\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-call-chain-throw-site-facts\",\"concept\":\"Static call chain + throw sites for a JVM primary class (what a stack trace should look like): per method its callees and the exceptions it throws, so a reported trace can be verified or derived\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 (unasked): Day26Variant000 main -> stageOne -> stageTwo -> stageThree (invokestatic), stageThree = `new java/lang/IllegalStateException` ... `athrow`; main compares HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL / HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT via ScriptBytecodeAdapter.compareEqual and catches the exception (trace effects bounded_caught_exception_only). Build from Code attributes: callees per method (invokestatic/virtual/special/interface; invokedynamic bootstrap names; Groovy dynamic call sites = the `$createCallSiteArray_1` string array when the class is not @CompileStatic), thrown classes (`new X` ... `athrow`, `athrow` of a param), exception_table (handler ranges + catch types), LineNumberTable lines per throw, `throws` (Exceptions attribute). Answers: fault_method from bytecode alone (the only method that athrows the trace kind), call depth, caller of X, catch site, line of the throw, `frames_are_call_chain` predicate. Same for Kotlin/Scala ($ module) /Clojure (invokeStatic) layouts; fixtures: D24/D25/D26 jars.\"},\n {\"id\":\"elf-core-dump-triage\",\"concept\":\"Native crash dump: ELF core file (ET_CORE) as a group member beside its executable -- signal, faulting RIP, registers, mapped files, fault address\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Natural native sequel to D26 ('the dump is a confession ... find the faulting instruction'). Parse PT_NOTE (owner CORE/LINUX): NT_PRSTATUS (pr_cursig, pr_pid, user_regs_struct order r15..rip,cs,eflags,rsp,ss,fs_base..), NT_PRPSINFO (pr_fname, pr_psargs), NT_SIGINFO (si_signo, si_errno, si_code SEGV_MAPERR=1/ACCERR=2, si_addr), NT_AUXV (AT_ENTRY, AT_PHDR, AT_EXECFN), NT_FILE (count, page_size, start/end/file_ofs + names), NT_FPREGSET; PT_LOAD memory for stack reads. Map RIP to (module, file offset) via NT_FILE and to a function via the companion member's symtab/.eh_frame (build-id NT_GNU_BUILD_ID match). Labels: signal names `SIGSEGV`/`SIGABRT`/`SIGFPE`/`SIGILL`/`SIGBUS`/`SIGTRAP` and numbers 11/6/8/4/7/5; hex with 0x. Fixtures: compile tiny C crashers (null write, div0, abort via __stack_chk_fail, ud2) and make cores with `gdb -batch -ex run -ex generate-core-file` on OUR fixtures only (never run a challenge sample); 32-bit + AArch64 cores via synthetic note writers.\"},\n {\"id\":\"faulting-instruction-locator\",\"concept\":\"'Find the faulting instruction': map a fault pc/offset (from a core, minidump, text report or the question) to its function and decode/classify the instruction\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Inputs: VA or file offset + member. Containing function via .symtab/.dynsym FUNC ranges, then .eh_frame FDE ranges (stripped), PE .pdata RUNTIME_FUNCTION, Mach-O LC_FUNCTION_STARTS; JVM: bytecode offset -> method via Code ranges + LineNumberTable. Decode with capstone intel in the GM convention (lowercase, decimal immediates, no trailing space: `mov dword ptr [rax], 0`), plus facts: mnemonic, memory operand base/index/disp, access size, read vs write, offset within function (`func+0x1a`). Classify: null-pointer read/write (base reg 0 / si_addr < 0x1000), divide error (`div`/`idiv`, SIGFPE), `ud2`/`int3`/`hlt` trap, call through bad pointer, stack-protector abort (`call __stack_chk_fail`), assert/abort. Fixtures from the elf-core-dump-triage crashers (x86-64, i386, AArch64).\"},\n {\"id\":\"static-stack-unwinder\",\"concept\":\"'Unwind the stack' statically: reconstruct the frame list from captured stack memory + the binary's unwind info, without executing anything\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"RBP-chain walk (saved rbp/ret pairs) over a core PT_LOAD or MDMP MemoryList range; CFI unwinding with pyelftools CallFrameInfo (decoded table: CFA rule + RA offset at a pc) for -fomit-frame-pointer code; PE x64 UNWIND_INFO (UWOP codes) from .pdata/.xdata; AArch64 x29/x30 chain. Output frames innermost-first as (module, symbol, offset) and per-function frame sizes (CFA offset at body). Fixtures: same crasher built -O0 (frame pointers) and -O2 -fomit-frame-pointer, plus a MinGW PE.\"},\n {\"id\":\"windows-minidump-triage\",\"concept\":\"Windows minidump (`MDMP`) as a crash member beside a PE: exception code/address, faulting thread context, module list\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure-Python parser: MINIDUMP_HEADER (`MDMP`, version 0xa793, NumberOfStreams, StreamDirectoryRva), streams ThreadList(3), ModuleList(4), MemoryList(5)/Memory64List(9), Exception(6: ThreadId, ExceptionCode, ExceptionFlags, ExceptionAddress, NumberParameters + info[0]=read0/write1/DEP8, info[1]=address), SystemInfo(7), MiscInfo(15). CONTEXT_AMD64 Rip/Rsp/Rbp at the documented offsets. Code names: 0xC0000005 EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION, 0xC0000094 INTEGER_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO, 0xC0000409 STACK_BUFFER_OVERRUN, 0x80000003 BREAKPOINT, 0xC000001D ILLEGAL_INSTRUCTION, 0xE06D7363 C++ EH, 0xE0434352 CLR. Map ExceptionAddress -> module + RVA -> function (exports/.pdata/COFF symbols). Fixtures: synthesise MDMP files with a writer (no Windows box).\"},\n {\"id\":\"text-crash-report-parsers\",\"concept\":\"Textual crash reports as members or sidecars: Java stack traces / hs_err_pid, .NET exception text, Go panic, Rust panic backtrace, Python traceback, sanitizer reports, glibc aborts, dmesg segfault lines\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Regex parsers -> {kind, message, frames[], fault_addr, access (READ/WRITE of size N), bug_class}: Java `Exception in thread \\\"main\\\" X: msg` + `\\\\tat a.b.C.m(F.java:12)` + `Caused by:`/`Suppressed:`/`... N more`; hs_err `SIGSEGV (0xb) at pc=..., pid=..`, `Problematic frame: C [libx.so+0x1234] f+0x14`; .NET `Unhandled exception. System.X: msg` + `at Ns.T.M() in f.cs:line 12`; Go `panic: runtime error: index out of range [5] with length 3` + `goroutine 1 [running]:` + `main.f(...)\\\\n\\\\t/p/f.go:12 +0x1d`; Rust `thread 'main' panicked at src/main.rs:4:5:` + numbered backtrace; Python Traceback (most recent call LAST = reverse order!); ASan `ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow on address 0x.. pc 0x.. bp sp`, `READ of size 4`, `#0 0x.. in f file.c:12:5`, `SUMMARY:`; UBSan `runtime error:`; glibc `*** stack smashing detected ***`, `free(): double free detected in tcache 2`; dmesg `segfault at 0 ip 0000.. sp .. error 4 in bin[55..+1000]`. Map bug kind -> CWE via vulnerability-class-classifier. Watch frame ORDER per format (innermost-first vs Python's outermost-first).\"},\n {\"id\":\"trace-symbolization-retrace\",\"concept\":\"Symbolize / de-obfuscate crash frames: ProGuard/R8 mapping.txt retrace, stripped addresses via a symbolized twin or build-id debug file, .NET portable PDB file:line\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Combines the D15 stripped/symbolized pair with D26 traces: frames like `a.a.b(Unknown Source)` + a `mapping.txt` member (`orig.Class -> a.a:` / `    12:15:void method():30:33 -> b` line-range maps, inlined frames expand to several), raw addresses / `bin+0x1136` in a stripped ELF resolved through the symbolized twin (same build-id/.text bytes) or a separate `.debug` file (`.gnu_debuglink` CRC32 / build-id path), .NET portable PDB (BSJB `#Pdb` stream, MethodDebugInformation sequence points) -> file:line. Fixtures: tiny ProGuard-style mapping + obfuscated jar names; D15 fixtures for the native side.\"},\n {\"id\":\"crash-exploitability-verdict\",\"concept\":\"Triage verdict for a crash: classify the fault (null deref, wild read/write, exec of non-code, stack overrun/canary, heap corruption abort, div0, assertion) and an !exploitable-style rating with the mitigations present\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Triage what went wrong from the wreckage' (D26 prompt) as fields: inputs = signal/exception code + si_code + fault address class (null page < 0x10000, non-canonical, stack, heap, mapped module, unmapped) + faulting insn class (read/write/exec/call-through-reg, from faulting-instruction-locator) + abort reason strings; outputs = fault_class token, CWE (476/787/125/121/122/415/416/369/617), rating EXPLOITABLE / PROBABLY_EXPLOITABLE / PROBABLY_NOT_EXPLOITABLE / UNKNOWN (CERT !exploitable / GDB exploitable rule order), mitigations (canary, NX, PIE, RELRO, FORTIFY, CFG) from the binary. The built crash-exploitability-facts covers stack frame geometry; this adds the verdict layer.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-niche-language-members\",\"concept\":\"Next JVM languages after Groovy as a new-day member: JRuby, Jython, Ceylon, Frege/Eta, Xtend, BeanShell/Kotlin script classes -- identity cues, primary classfile, where the base64 HCFG string lives\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D22-D26 = 5 'new language on an old runtime' days (F#, VB.NET, Scala, Clojure, Groovy). Cues: JRuby AOT `org/jruby/` refs + `RUBY$method$` names; Jython `$py.class` + `org/python/core/PyFunctionTable`, constants via `PyString.fromInterned`; Ceylon `com/redhat/ceylon` + `$module_` classes; Frege `frege/runtime`; Xtend plain Java + `org/eclipse/xtext/xbase/lib`; Kotlin script `*_main.kts`-style `ScriptTemplateWithArgs`. All label `jar`; HCFG = constant-pool base64 >= 80 chars in whichever class holds it (scan all classes, not just Main-Class). Fixtures: hand-built classfiles with the right refs (no compilers installed).\"},\n]\nids={x['id'] for x in g}\nfor x in new: assert x['id'] not in ids, x['id']\n# insert new P1s after the first note, others appended by priority\nout=[]\np1=[x for x in new if x['priority']==1]; rest=[x for x in new if x['priority']!=1]\nfor idx,x in enumerate(g):\n    out.append(x)\n    if idx==0: pass\n# order: all P1 first (new P1 at top), then P2 (new P2 first), then P3\ndef key(x): return x['priority']\nnewids={x['id'] for x in new}\nfinal=sorted(new+g, key=lambda x:(x['priority'], 0 if x['id'] in newids else 1))\nbody='\\n'+'[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x, ensure_ascii=False) for x in final)+'\\n]\\n'\nt=t[:j]+body+t[k:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n# validate\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=t.index('```json',i)+7; k=t.index('```',j)\ngg=json.loads(t[j:k]); print(len(gg), all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in gg))\ns=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in gg if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (s.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or s.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pend), pend)\nEOF","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps JSON with new prebuild gaps"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1508,"cache_read_input_tokens":149996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1508},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10275bf2-3967-4c85-8fd5-58c86d81240b","uuid":"948240a7-3179-4308-afc0-ed483809dc2d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:12:42.072Z","request_id":"req_011CgQuRrJoYiNtFnrVz4bHP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LVqyPUJC7zr6CrRpVsgTK4":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=t.index('```json',i)+len('```json'); k=t.index('```',j)\ng=json.loads(t[j:k])\nbyid={x['id']:x for x in g}\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='groovy-script-class-facts']   # seen day26\nbyid['solver-member-cache-identity']['priority']=2\nbyid['solver-member-cache-identity']['detail']+=\" D26: the fix held -- Mastery 10 sets (3120 ids) and TT CORRECT first try; keep the regression and re-check after any set-count jump.\"\nbyid['contract-forward-hints']['detail']+=\" D26: the d07 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit' leak came TRUE (Groovy jar; the primary classfile = the manifest Main-Class `Day26Variant000`, not the `$_main_closure1` closure). Only `neko_bytecode` remains open; D26 contract added no new token/day.\"\nbyid['theme-facts-recording']['detail']+=\" D26: the theme WAS asked on its own day again (first since D20): crash_fau